From: djnice <djnice77@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AMLCodec: end a drain whose pictures stopped coming

In a drain GetPicture returned VC_NONE as long as the amlvideo queue held a
picture. When the last pictures stop leaving the video layer, e.g. playback
stopped right at the end of a file while composed FEL frames still wait there
(P7_FEL_STDL1: the dvfel waits for the missing EL of the last pictures, so its
drain takes longer), the player sat in its 40 s drain timeout before the next
file could start. End the drain after 2 s without a picture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
index d9e2f0f..92981cd 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
@@ -3086,6 +3086,16 @@ CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn CAMLCodec::GetPicture(VideoPicture *pVideoPicture)
   }
   else if (m_drain && m_buffer_level_ready && (queued_frames == 0))
     return CDVDVideoCodec::VC_EOF;
+  // The last pictures can stop leaving the video layer during the drain, e.g.
+  // when playback is stopped right at the end of a file while composed FEL
+  // frames still wait there: VC_NONE then held the player until its 40 s drain
+  // timeout. Pictures come out at the frame rate while a drain makes progress.
+  else if (m_drain && m_buffer_level_ready && elapsed_since_last_frame > std::chrono::seconds(2))
+  {
+    CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "CAMLCodec::GetPicture: drain without a picture for {:d} ms, {:d} queued: done",
+              elapsed_since_last_frame.count(), queued_frames);
+    return CDVDVideoCodec::VC_EOF;
+  }
   else if ((m_drain && m_buffer_level_ready) || (buffer_level > (streambuffer ? 100.0f : 10.0f)))
     return CDVDVideoCodec::VC_NONE;
   else if (ret != EAGAIN || elapsed_since_last_frame > std::chrono::seconds(m_decoder_timeout))
